1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,254
A paid order still has to be packed and sent.

2
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:09,232
This video shows how to create shipments, ship in parts, follow a parcel

3
00:00:09,232 --> 00:00:13,890
to delivery or return, set up EasyPost labels, and what buyers see.

4
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:21,342
An order is not finished when it is paid.

5
00:00:21,342 --> 00:00:25,590
Someone has to pack it, send it, and tell the buyer where it is.

6
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:30,127
Shipping part of an order, or one parcel at a time, is hard

7
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:32,050
to follow in a spreadsheet.

8
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:37,356
Shipments record what is in each parcel, the carrier and the tracking number,

9
00:00:37,356 --> 00:00:40,430
so you always know what has left and what is left.

10
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:45,394
The buyer is emailed when a parcel leaves, and sees it on their order.

11
00:00:45,394 --> 00:00:48,000
With EasyPost, you can buy the label too.

12
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:58,130
A paid order with goods has a Shipments section on its page, under Commerce, Orders.

13
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:03,787
A shipment says which items are in a parcel, and the carrier and tracking number.

14
00:01:03,787 --> 00:01:06,100
It starts Being packed, or Shipped.

15
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:10,848
Then it is Delivered, or Returned if it comes back, and its items

16
00:01:10,848 --> 00:01:12,200
can be sent again.

17
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:17,490
A shipment still being packed can be removed, which puts its items back.

18
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,811
Open an order that is paid.

19
00:01:23,811 --> 00:01:28,038
Under New shipment, set how many of each item go in the parcel.

20
00:01:28,038 --> 00:01:30,242
All that is left is filled in.

21
00:01:30,242 --> 00:01:32,570
Lower a number to ship in parts.

22
00:01:33,028 --> 00:01:35,795
Enter the Carrier and the Tracking number.

23
00:01:35,795 --> 00:01:39,945
The Tracking link is optional, and the Note is for the store only.

24
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:44,498
Leave It has left, mark it shipped now ticked, and click Create shipment.

25
00:01:50,275 --> 00:01:53,855
The shipment is listed with what is in it, the carrier and the

26
00:01:53,855 --> 00:01:57,276
tracking link, and the order now reads Partially fulfilled.

27
00:01:57,276 --> 00:01:59,855
The buyer is emailed that it is on its way.

28
00:02:04,056 --> 00:02:07,979
Untick It has left to set the items aside while they are packed.

29
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:10,277
The shipment shows as Being packed.

30
00:02:10,277 --> 00:02:14,761
Each shipment has a packing slip button, which prints its items and number

31
00:02:14,761 --> 00:02:16,106
to put in the box.

32
00:02:16,557 --> 00:02:20,199
Mark shipped sends it later, and the buyer is emailed then.

33
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:23,057
A shipment still being packed can be removed.

34
00:02:23,507 --> 00:02:26,822
When the carrier says it arrived, click Delivered.

35
00:02:26,822 --> 00:02:29,130
If it comes back, click Returned:

36
00:02:29,130 --> 00:02:32,917
its items count as not shipped, so they can be sent again.

37
00:02:37,102 --> 00:02:42,014
With the EasyPost feature, the shipping settings have an EasyPost tab for your

38
00:02:42,014 --> 00:02:46,458
account's key, and a Sending parcels tab for the address you ship from

39
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:48,036
and your default box.

40
00:02:48,036 --> 00:02:50,492
This demo does not contact EasyPost.

41
00:02:52,092 --> 00:02:56,999
Offer the carriers' rates at checkout by adding a Carrier rates method to a zone.

42
00:02:56,999 --> 00:02:59,312
The buyer sees each carrier's rate.

43
00:03:00,062 --> 00:03:03,391
Create the shipment being packed, and click Buy label.

44
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:08,217
Your EasyPost account is charged, the shipment is marked shipped with the carrier

45
00:03:08,217 --> 00:03:11,102
and tracking number, and the buyer is emailed.

46
00:03:11,852 --> 00:03:16,736
Once registered, the carrier's latest word, such as In transit, shows on the

47
00:03:16,736 --> 00:03:21,382
shipment, and a parcel the carrier delivers is marked Delivered for you.

48
00:03:25,572 --> 00:03:28,353
Customers see their shipments under My Orders.

49
00:03:28,353 --> 00:03:32,097
A guest uses the order link, or Track your order, with the order

50
00:03:32,097 --> 00:03:34,932
number and the email the order was placed with.

51
00:03:35,737 --> 00:03:38,966
Both must match, so a number alone shows nothing.

52
00:03:38,966 --> 00:03:43,367
The order lists each shipment with the carrier and the tracking link.

53
00:03:47,567 --> 00:03:53,874
With Workflows on, the Shipment Created, Shipped, Delivered and Returned events start workflows,

54
00:03:53,874 --> 00:03:57,027
for example to tell a warehouse or a carrier.

55
00:03:57,777 --> 00:04:02,117
The shipped email is on by default, and needs an email service.

56
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:07,477
Each shipment has its own packing slip, which lists only its items.

57
00:04:08,227 --> 00:04:14,587
The Shipping times report shows how long orders waited and how long deliveries took, by carrier.

58
00:04:18,787 --> 00:04:20,160
An order in parts:

59
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,707
ship what is in stock now, and the rest when it arrives.

60
00:04:24,457 --> 00:04:25,914
A packing station:

61
00:04:25,914 --> 00:04:30,527
create shipments being packed, print the slips, and mark them shipped.

62
00:04:31,277 --> 00:04:33,842
Labels without leaving the order:

63
00:04:33,842 --> 00:04:36,077
buy and print with EasyPost.

64
00:04:36,827 --> 00:04:38,492
A return in the post:

65
00:04:38,492 --> 00:04:41,697
mark the shipment returned, and send it again.

66
00:04:43,697 --> 00:04:48,853
Record every parcel, follow it to the door, and let buyers track their order.

67
00:04:48,853 --> 00:04:50,467
Thanks for watching.

